ESP_Octopus
- Board role: Wi-Fi access point, web portal, Octopus serial bridge, Marlin lamp controller
- Wi-Fi AP SSID: ESP_Octopus
- Wi-Fi AP password: octopus123
- Fixed IP: 192.168.4.1
- UART to Octopus board:
  - ESP32 `GPIO16` (RX) -> Octopus WIFI header pin 15 -> `PD8` (`USART3_TX`, often labeled `ESP-RX` on the board docs)
  - ESP32 `GPIO17` (TX) -> Octopus WIFI header pin 16 -> `PD9` (`USART3_RX`, often labeled `ESP-TX` on the board docs)
  - Current Marlin mapping: ESP uses Octopus WIFI header `USART3` on `PD8` / `PD9` at `115200`
- Octopus hardware reset line:
  - GPIO23 -> Octopus RESET pin
  - Drive style: open-drain, active-low pulse
  - Wiring rule: common GND required
- Lamp control:
  - no local lamp PWM pin on the ESP32
  - sends `M355` to Marlin
  - Marlin drives the configured Octopus bed/heater output

ESP_Remote
- Board role: handheld remote with 7 push buttons, fixed-IP Wi-Fi client
- Fixed IP: 192.168.4.2
- Gateway / ESP_Octopus IP: 192.168.4.1
- Buttons use INPUT_PULLUP and are active-low:
  - GPIO13 -> Lights On
  - GPIO14 -> Lights Off
  - GPIO25 -> Pos1
  - GPIO26 -> Pos2
  - GPIO27 -> Random Position
  - GPIO32 -> Dimmer / hold-to-change-brightness
  - GPIO33 -> Spare / reserved

